<string name="diag_usb_direct_eq_desc">Source (%1$d Hz) = DAC Stream (%2$d Hz / %3$dbit) → USB Host direct write, bypasses AudioFlinger, true bit-perfect output</string>
<string name="diag_oboe_exclusive_mmap">Oboe Exclusive · MMAP Direct</string>
<string name="diag_oboe_exclusive_desc">Source (%1$d Hz) → Oboe Exclusive bypasses Android Mixer. Non-USB direct write, not labeled Bit-Perfect.</string>
<string name="diag_aaudio_shared">AAudio Shared · System Mixer In Path</string>
<string name="diag_aaudio_shared_desc">In Shared mode AudioFlinger forces all audio streams to resample to device native rate. Even if the app layer does not resample, the system mixer still performs SRC internally.\n\nSuggestion: switch to Oboe Exclusive mode for true bit-perfect output.</string>
<string name="diag_app_resampling">App-layer resampling in progress</string>
<string name="diag_app_resampling_desc">Audio is being resampled from source rate to device native rate. Resampling happens in the Oboe/AAudio layer as software SRC, does not affect quality.</string>
<string name="diag_about_page">About This Page</string>
<string name="diag_explanation">• Live Monitor — polls getSharingMode() every second, detects system preemption/downgrade\n• AF Track Flags — AudioFlinger low-level track flags (0x000=Shared, 0x100=MMAP, 0x004=Direct)\n• Focus Events — audio focus change log, shows system audio preemption timeline\n• Bit-Perfect only holds under USB DAC Exclusive direct write: bypasses AudioFlinger and Mixer\n• Under AAudio Shared mode AudioFlinger always participates, internal resampling uncontrollable</string>
